    {"idle.watch", "Watch for the session being idle for `seconds` and return the IdleWatch. Any number of watches can exist, up to 256 for each runtime, each with its own time. The watch exists at once, not idle; if the compositor refuses it, it ends and its \"closed\" listeners get the reason.", api_params_44, 1, "IdleWatch"},
    {"input.current_source", "Return the selected input source, or nil when there is no current source.", NULL, 0, "InputSource|nil"},
    {"input.devices", "Return available input devices.", NULL, 0, "InputDevice[]"},
    {"input.grab", "Take the keyboard and return the Grab. The Grab exists at once; if the compositor refuses it (the session is locked, or a modal or capture_input shortcut session or a shortcut capture holds the keyboard, or any key is held down), it ends and its \"closed\" listeners get the reason. A key held when a grab starts would have its release go to the grab, and the focused application would never see the key lift, so the compositor refuses a grab while a key is down: start it from a key release, or later. The grab starts with its timeout running, so renew it if the script has nothing to receive for a while. Call this while handling an event, as with every operation.", api_params_47, 1, "Grab"},
    {"input.on", "Register a Lua policy callback for matching input events. The Subscription it returns has the same shape as the one of gnoblin.on and of every object's on: sub:unsubscribe() removes the handler, and input that matched it goes on to the next handler or the application. A handler cannot be added or removed from inside an input callback.", api_params_48, 2, "Subscription"},
