    {"settings.override", "Layer a value over one committed setting, for this runtime, and return the Override. The path is \"section.key\" with the names of the configuration, such as `window_management.focus_mode`. Only a setting that can change while the session runs is accepted: `window_management.*`, `compositor.*`, `cursor.theme`, `cursor.size`, `layer_shell.preserve_active_window`, `monitors.privacy_screen` and `input.orientation_lock`. Any other path raises an error that says why it cannot change at runtime. The value is checked the way the configuration checks it, so a value the configuration would refuse raises an error too. The orientation lock and the privacy screen take `true` or `false`; a privacy screen needs an output that has one. If the compositor refuses the override, it ends and its \"closed\" listeners get the reason. Call this while handling an event, as with every operation.", api_params_79, 2, "Override"},
